# Front-office SEO (Blade)

End-user pages use **Laravel Blade** with layout [`resources/views/layouts/front.blade.php`](resources/views/layouts/front.blade.php). Document `<title>`, meta, Open Graph, Twitter, hreflang, and JSON-LD are rendered **server-side** via [`resources/views/partials/seo-head.blade.php`](resources/views/partials/seo-head.blade.php) from the `$seo` array built by [`Modules\Base\Support\FrontSeo`](Modules/Base/app/Support/FrontSeo.php).

## Where global SEO lives

[`FrontViewData`](Modules/Base/app/Support/FrontViewData.php) (via `FrontLayoutComposer`) shares on every front view:

| Key | Purpose |
|-----|--------|
| `globals.seo` | Localized key/value rows from `Modules\Base\Models\Seo` |
| `globals.media` | Resolved public URLs, including `meta_img` |
| `globals.about` / `globals.turkish_citizenship` | Section copy + meta fields |
| `locale_switcher` | `[{code, native, url}, …]` for en/tr/ar → hreflang |
| `appName` | Website name |

Controllers pass page-specific SEO with `FrontSeo::make(...)`, `FrontSeo::forHome(...)`, or `FrontSeo::forHub(...)`.

## Page tiers (convention)

### 1) Global / hub pages

Home, listings index, marketing hubs.

- Prefer `FrontSeo::forHome` / `FrontSeo::forHub` + `globals.seo` fallbacks.
- Canonical = hub route URL (no noisy query strings unless required).

### 2) Parent / section pages

About Us, Turkish citizenship, CMS pages.

- Defaults from `globals`; overrides from controller props when non-empty.

### 3) Detail pages

Property show, blog article.

- Title/description/keywords from the **entity**.
- OG image from entity media; fall back to `globals.media.meta_img`.
- Property: include RealEstateListing + BreadcrumbList + admin `metadata.schema` in `json_ld`.
- Blog: `og:type=article` + Article JSON-LD via `StructuredData`.

## Implementation checklist

1. Return `view('…::front.…')` with `'seo' => FrontSeo::…`.
2. Do not rely on client JS for head tags — crawlers must see them in View Source.
3. Keep hreflang (en/tr/ar + x-default) via `locale_switcher` inside `FrontSeo::make`.
4. Use `StructuredData` PHP builders (not the old Vue `structuredData.js`).

